<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 25 May, from 1085 to 1977.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1085</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfonso VI of Castile takes Toledo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alfonso VI entered Toledo after its Muslim ruler surrendered. The old Visigothic capital became a centre where Christian, Jewish and Muslim scholars translated Arabic learning into Latin.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1521</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles V issues the Edict of Worms against Luther</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The emperor declared Martin Luther an outlaw and banned his writings. Protected by Frederick the Wise at the Wartburg, Luther began translating the New Testament into German.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1787</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constitutional Convention opens in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates reached a quorum at the Pennsylvania State House and chose George Washington to preside. Over the summer they drafted the US Constitution.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1803</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ralph Waldo Emerson is born in Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emerson became the leading voice of Transcendentalism. Essays such as 'Self-Reliance' shaped American thought and influenced Thoreau and Whitman.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1961</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy commits America to landing on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Addressing Congress, President Kennedy called for a man to be landed on the Moon and returned safely before the decade was out. Apollo 11 met the goal in July 1969.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1977</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Star Wars opens in American cinemas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Lucas's space adventure opened in a few dozen cinemas and became the highest-grossing film to that date. It reshaped Hollywood around the blockbuster and merchandising.</p></li></ol>
